# Post-processing scripts

R scripts producing the figures in Corbier et al., *Beyond Ownership: Sufficiency and inequality shape product-sharing’s environmental potential*.

These read **model output**, not the model itself. Run CIRCEE first (see the main README), then point these scripts at the resulting files.

---

## Inputs

| Input | Produced by |
| --- | --- |
| `<behavioural>_AE_<scenario>.csv` — one per run, wide format (`Row`, `Y2018`, `Y2019`, …) | `src/CIRCEE_RunFile.m` |
| `NoModifiers_AE.csv` — the reference run | `src/CIRCEE_RunFile.m`, all modifiers at zero |
| `welfare_CEV_lifetime.csv` and the other welfare CSVs | `src/CIRCEE_WelfarePostProcess.m` |
| `shocks_final_<behavioural>_<scenario>.csv` — long format (`Variable`; `Region`; `Year`; `Value`) | the coupled pipeline, `scripts/run.sh` |

### What the filenames encode

Two dimensions vary across runs: the infrastructures configurations (the substitution elasticity path) and the behavioural modifiers (the behavioural configuration). Filenames encode both, and `Baseline` refers to the infrastructures with the presence of lifestyle heterogeneity.

| File | Behavioural modifiers | Infrastructures
| --- | --- | --- |
| `NoModifiers_AE.csv` | Behavioural modifiers all zero — the reference run | Current enablement
| `<behavioural>_AE_Baseline.csv`| Behavioural modifiers active| Current enablement
| `<behavioural>_AE_Progressive.csv`| Behavioural modifiers active | Broad enablement
| `<behavioural>_AE_Regressive.csv`| Behavioural modifiers active | Concentrated enablement

`AE` denotes anticipation errors. `<behavioural>` is one of `ecoactive_ecoactive`, `affordability_affordability`, `ecoactive_affordability`, `affordability_ecoactive` — sharing driver followed by sufficiency driver.
For example, `ecoactive_affordability`, reads as Ecoactive - Sharing x Affordability - Sufficiency.

Twelve scenario runs are expected (four behavioural configurations × three infrastructures), plus the reference run.

**All figures report changes relative to `NoModifiers_AE.csv`**: the BAU infrastructures with no behavioural modifiers active (no lifestyle heterogeneity).

### Code tokens vs. paper labels

| Code token | Paper label |
| --- | --- |
| `Baseline` | Current enablement |
| `Progressive` | Broad enablement |
| `Regressive` | Concentrated enablement |
| `NoModifiers` | reference run |
| `lowcarbon` | Higher income |
| `cautious` | Medium income |
| `constrained` | Lower income |

Lifestyle group names describe archetypes from Pettifor et al. (2023) rather than income deciles; the income ordering is a property of the groups, not their definition.

### Setting the paths

Set the input and output directories at the top of each script:

```r
levels_dir <- "path/to/CIRCEE_output_levels"
out_dir    <- "path/to/figures"
```

